From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:24:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 089/110] Select and copy text in the Markdown preview

Paragraphs, headings, list items, code lines and table cells of the
preview can be selected with the mouse, across blocks as in a browser.
Ctrl+C in the Preview view copies the selected rendered text, or nothing
when none is selected, never the hidden editor's selection. Ctrl+A
selects the whole rendered document. Escape or a click elsewhere clears.
In the Split view the editor keeps its own selection; Copy takes the
preview's while it has one. A click without a drag still follows a link
and a <details> summary still toggles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

